2. bxc5 Kf7 3. g4 $1 { This space-clearer had to be anticipated when offering the exchange of queens. } ( { After } 3. Kg2 $2 Ke6 4. Kf3 Kd5 5. g4 hxg4 6. Kxg4 Kxc5 { Black makes a draw. } ) 
 ( { But } 3. Kh3 { first also worked, for example } f5 { (else 4. g4 decides) followed by } 4. Kg2 { and the king soon reaches g5. } ) 
hxg4 4. Kg3 f5 5. Kf4 Ke6 6. c6 ( { Also good is } 6. Kg5 Kd5 7. h5 $1 gxh5 8. Kxh5 Kxc5 9. Kg5 { and after taking the second pawn, White's king will find itself on a key square. } ) 
Kd6 7. h5 $1 gxh5 8. Kxf5 Kxc6 9. Kg5 Kd6 10. Kxh5 g3 ( { Or } 10... Ke5 11. Kxg4 Kf6 12. Kf4 { etc. } ) 
11. fxg3 Ke6 12. Kg6 
